---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import UnitFinder from '../components/UnitFinder.astro';


const whatsappUrl = 'https://wa.me/447916696894';
const siteUrl = 'https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com';

const nhsGuide = { text: 'guide to CMI qualifications for NHS managers', href: `${siteUrl}/guides/nhs-management-cmi-qualifications/` };
const commandVerbsGuide = { text: 'guide to CMI command verbs', href: `${siteUrl}/guides/cmi-command-verbs-explained/` };
const harvardGuide = { text: 'Harvard referencing guide for CMI assignments', href: `${siteUrl}/guides/harvard-referencing-cmi/` };

// One list drives both the visible FAQ and the FAQ JSON-LD, so the two always match.
// Each answer is a list of paragraphs. A paragraph is a list of plain strings and { text, href } links.
const faqGroups = [
  {
    id: 'getting-started',
    label: 'Getting Started',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Which CMI levels and units do you cover?',
        a: [[
          'All five CMI qualification levels: Level 3 Principles of Management and Leadership (Units 301–321), Level 4 Management and Leadership (Units 4001–4009, 5001, 5012 and 5014), Level 5 Management and Leadership Diploma (Units 501–526), Level 6 Professional Management and Leadership (Units 601–614), and Level 7 Strategic Management and Leadership (Units 701–716). That covers all 80+ CMI units across every Award, Certificate, and Diploma pathway.',
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'What does the CMI assignment writing service include?',
        a: [[
          "A complete, submission-ready assignment written to the correct command verb depth for your unit and level. This includes the required CMI format (management report or structured essay), Harvard referencing with sources chosen to support each assessment criterion (the unit specifications don't set a minimum number of sources), and precise alignment to the Learning Outcomes and Assessment Criteria of your specific unit. All documents are written by UK-based CMI-qualified practitioners.",
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'Do you provide CMI assignment help for NHS managers?',
        a: [[
          'Yes. NHS managers study CMI qualifications at several levels, and the right level depends on the scope of your role rather than your pay band. Support covers NHS workforce context and leadership frameworks. See our ',
          nhsGuide,
          '.',
        ]],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'assessments-grading',
    label: 'Assessments & Grading',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'How are CMI assignments graded?',
        a: [[
          'CMI grades its qualifications Pass or Refer, with no Merit or Distinction. A Pass means every assessment criterion in the unit has been met.',
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'What do command verbs like Analyse and Evaluate mean?',
        a: [[
          'Each assessment criterion starts with a command verb, and meeting the criterion means doing what that verb asks. For example, Evaluate asks you to weigh strengths and weaknesses and reach a stated conclusion. See our ',
          commandVerbsGuide,
          '.',
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'What word count should my assignment be?',
        a: [[
          "Word counts by level are: Level 3, 2,000–2,500; Level 4, 3,000; Level 5, 3,000–5,000; Level 6, 3,000–4,000; and Level 7, 3,500–4,500. Your centre's assessment brief has the final say.",
        ]],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'referencing-originality',
    label: 'Referencing & Originality',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Which referencing style should I use?',
        a: [[
          "CMI's syllabuses don't name a referencing style. Harvard is commonly used, so follow your centre's guide and use one version throughout. See our ",
          harvardGuide,
          '.',
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'How many sources do I need?',
        a: [[
          "CMI's unit specifications set no minimum number of sources. They ask for appropriate use of evidence, examples and references to support conclusions and recommendations.",
        ]],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'resubmissions',
    label: 'Resubmissions',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Does a Refer mean I have failed?',
        a: [[
          'No. A Refer is not a final fail. It means the evidence did not yet show that every assessment criterion was met. The usual next step is to correct the gaps the assessor identified and resubmit. Your centre explains what happens next.',
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'What happens if my CMI assignment receives a Refer?',
        a: [
          [
            'A Refer means the assignment did not meet one or more Learning Outcomes at the required command verb depth. Our resubmission support identifies which Learning Outcomes were unmet, reads the assessor feedback, and either rewrites the relevant sections (writing service) or guides you through the restructure (tutoring). The most common causes of a CMI Refer are insufficient command verb depth (for example, describing where the brief demanded Evaluate) and under-referenced analysis sections.',
          ],
          ['Message us on WhatsApp with your original submission and assessor feedback for resubmission support.'],
        ],
      },
      {
        q: "How do I use my assessor's feedback?",
        a: [[
          'List the criteria not yet met, read each comment against the wording of the criterion, then write a one-line change for each before you start rewriting.',
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'How many resubmission attempts do I get, and by when?',
        a: [[
          "CMI's syllabuses set no standard resubmission window or number of attempts. Your centre decides, so ask it in writing. The Level 4, 6 and 7 syllabuses state a five-year registration period for all assessment.",
        ]],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'ordering-policies',
    label: 'Ordering & Policies',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'How do I place an order for CMI assignment help?',
        a: [[
          'Message us on WhatsApp with your unit number, qualification level, assignment brief, and deadline. We respond with a fixed quote within 2 hours and assign a CMI-qualified writer matched to your level and unit subject. See the CMI assignment help online page for full process details.',
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'What is the difference between the writing service and CMI assignment tutoring?',
        a: [[
          'The writing service produces a complete, submission-ready document written by a CMI-qualified practitioner on your behalf. CMI assignment tutoring retains your authorship. The tutor guides you through structure, command verb application, Learning Outcome alignment, and argument construction so that you produce the document. Tutoring is also the primary route for resubmission coaching after a Refer grade.',
        ]],
      },
      {
        q: 'Are you affiliated with CMI?',
        a: [[
          'No. cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com is an independent service, not affiliated with or endorsed by the Chartered Management Institute.',
        ]],
      },
    ],
  },
];

const faqParaText = (para) => para.map((part) => (typeof part === 'string' ? part : part.text)).join('');

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": faqGroups.flatMap((group) => group.items).map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": item.q,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": item.a.map(faqParaText).join(' ')
    }
  }))
};

const levels = [
  {
    label: 'CMI Level 3',
    icon: 'users',
    tone: 'green',
    title: 'Principles of Management and Leadership',
    slug: 'https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-3-assignment-help/',
    units: 'Units 301–321',
    format: '2,000–2,500 words guideline',
    verbs: 'Explain, Identify, Outline',
    profile: 'Team leaders and supervisors',
    badge: null,
  },
  {
    label: 'CMI Level 4',
    icon: 'clipboard',
    tone: 'blue',
    title: 'Management and Leadership',
    slug: 'https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-4-assignment-help/',
    units: 'Units 4001–4009',
    format: '3,000 words guideline',
    verbs: 'Describe, Discuss, Identify',
    profile: 'Junior and department managers',
    badge: null,
  },
  {
    label: 'CMI Level 5',
    icon: 'chart',
    tone: 'purple',
    title: 'Management & Leadership Diploma',
    slug: 'https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-5-assignment-help/',
    units: 'Units 501–526',
    format: '3,000–5,000 words guideline',
    verbs: 'Analyse, Examine, Evaluate',
    profile: 'Managers accountable to a senior manager',
    badge: null,
  },
  {
    label: 'CMI Level 6',
    icon: 'compass',
    tone: 'pink',
    title: 'Professional Management and Leadership',
    slug: 'https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-6-assignment-help/',
    units: 'Units 601–614',
    format: '3,000–4,000 words guideline',
    verbs: 'Critically appraise, Critically assess',
    profile: 'Experienced managers',
    badge: null,
  },
  {
    label: 'CMI Level 7',
    icon: 'flag',
    tone: 'orange',
    title: 'Strategic Management and Leadership',
    slug: 'https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-7-assignment-help/',
    units: 'Units 701–716',
    format: '3,500–4,500 words guideline',
    verbs: 'Critically appraise, Discuss, Develop',
    profile: 'Senior managers and directors',
    badge: null,
  },
];

const services = [
  {
    icon: 'pen',
    tone: 'blue',
    title: 'CMI Assignment Writing Service',
    href: `${siteUrl}/cmi-assignment-writing-service/`,
    desc: 'Submission-ready assignment written to the correct command verb depth and the format your centre sets, with full Harvard referencing.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'cap',
    tone: 'purple',
    title: 'CMI Assignment Tutoring',
    href: `${siteUrl}/cmi-assignment-tutoring/`,
    desc: 'Expert guidance for students writing their own assignment: structure planning, command verb application, Learning Outcome alignment, and resubmission coaching after a Referral.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'layers',
    tone: 'pink',
    title: 'CMI Coursework Help',
    href: `${siteUrl}/cmi-coursework-help/`,
    desc: 'Sustained support across multiple units of a full CMI Diploma, with consistent academic framing and command verb depth throughout the qualification.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'loop',
    tone: 'orange',
    title: 'CMI Resubmission Support',
    href: `${siteUrl}/guides/cmi-resubmission-guide/`,
    desc: 'Referral recovery: identifying unmet Learning Outcomes from assessor feedback, restructuring the response, and meeting the required command verb depth.',
  },
];

// Simple line icons, drawn inline (24 x 24 grid, stroked in the badge colour).
const serviceIcons: Record<string, string> = {
  pen: '<path d="M4 20l1.2-4.2L16.6 4.4a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 3 3L8.2 18.8z"/><path d="M14.5 6.5l3 3"/>',
  cap: '<path d="M2.5 9.5L12 5l9.5 4.5L12 14z"/><path d="M6.5 11.8V16c0 1.2 2.5 2.5 5.5 2.5s5.5-1.3 5.5-2.5v-4.2"/><path d="M21.5 9.5V14"/>',
  layers: '<path d="M12 3.5l9 4.5-9 4.5L3 8z"/><path d="M3 12l9 4.5 9-4.5"/><path d="M3 16l9 4.5 9-4.5"/>',
  loop: '<path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-3-6.7L21 8"/><path d="M21 3v5h-5"/>',
  users: '<circle cx="9" cy="8" r="3.2"/><path d="M3 20c0-3.3 2.7-6 6-6s6 2.7 6 6"/><path d="M16 5.2a3.2 3.2 0 0 1 0 5.6"/><path d="M18 14.3c2 .7 3.5 2.7 3.5 5.7"/>',
  clipboard: '<rect x="5" y="4.5" width="14" height="16.5" rx="2"/><path d="M9 3h6v3H9z"/><path d="M8.5 13.5l2.5 2.5 4.5-5"/>',
  chart: '<path d="M4 4v16h16"/><path d="M8 16v-4"/><path d="M12 16V8"/><path d="M16 16v-6"/>',
  compass: '<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M15.5 8.5l-2 5-5 2 2-5z"/>',
  flag: '<path d="M5 21V4"/><path d="M5 4h12l-2.5 4 2.5 4H5"/>',
  award: '<circle cx="12" cy="9" r="5.5"/><path d="M8.5 13.5L7 21l5-3 5 3-1.5-7.5"/>',
  target: '<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.2"/>',
  pin: '<path d="M12 21s7-6.2 7-11.5A7 7 0 0 0 5 9.5C5 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/>',
  book: '<path d="M12 6.5C10.5 5 8 4.5 4 4.5v14c4 0 6.5.5 8 2 1.5-1.5 4-2 8-2v-14c-4 0-6.5.5-8 2z"/><path d="M12 6.5v14"/>',
};

const steps = [
  { n: '01', text: 'Message us on WhatsApp with your unit number, level, and deadline.' },
  { n: '02', text: 'Receive a fixed quote within 2 hours, no hidden fees.' },
  { n: '03', text: 'We match you with a CMI-qualified UK writer at your exact level.' },
  { n: '04', text: 'Receive your submission-ready CMI assignment before your deadline.' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="CMI Assignment Help UK - Support & Guidance for Levels 3 to 7 | CMIAssignmentHelp.uk.com"
  description="Expert CMI assignment help for working professionals at Levels 3 to 7. UK-based CMI-qualified writers, all 80+ units covered. WhatsApp order in minutes."
  canonical={siteUrl + '/'}
  pageSchema={faqSchema}
>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       HERO — macro context, WhatsApp CTA above fold
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <p class="hero-eyebrow">UK-Based CMI Writers — All Levels 3 to 7</p>
        <h1 class="hero-h1">CMI Assignment Help UK</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          Expert CMI assignment writing, tutoring, and resubmission support for working
          professionals across all 80+ CMI units. Every document written to the correct
          command verb depth, so each criterion can be met.
        </p>
        <UnitFinder />
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a
            href={whatsappUrl}
            class="btn btn-whatsapp hero-wa"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Get a WhatsApp Quote
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">Fixed quote in 2 hours &bull; All 5 CMI qualification levels &bull; UK-based writers</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       SERVICES — service type disambiguation
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title services-title" id="cmi-assignment-support-services">Why Choose CMIAssignmentHelp.uk.com for CMI Assignment Support?</h2>
      <p class="section-lead services-lead">
        Four ways we support CMI learners, from a complete written assignment to guidance on your own draft or structured help across a full Diploma.
      </p>
      <p class="section-lead services-lead services-note">
        Everything is delivered remotely: see how <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-assignment-help-online/">CMI assignment help online</a> works.
      </p>
      <div class="services-grid">
        {services.map(svc => (
          <a href={svc.href} class={`service-card svc-${svc.tone}`}>
            <span class="svc-badge" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="svc-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false" set:html={serviceIcons[svc.icon]}></svg>
            </span>
            <h3 class="svc-title">{svc.title}</h3>
            <p class="svc-desc">{svc.desc}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       LEVEL NAVIGATION — qualification framework
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section" id="levels">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cmi-assignment-help-by-level">Choose Your CMI Level</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Select your CMI qualification level for level-specific assignment writing, tutoring, and unit-by-unit support.
        Every level has distinct command verb requirements, format standards, and word count targets. Our writers are
        matched to your exact level.
      </p>
      <div class="level-grid">
        {levels.map(lvl => (
          <div class={`level-card tone-${lvl.tone}`}>
            <span class="badge-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="svc-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false" set:html={serviceIcons[lvl.icon]}></svg>
            </span>
            {lvl.badge && <span class="level-badge">{lvl.badge}</span>}
            <h3 class="level-title"><a href={lvl.slug} class="card-link">{lvl.label} assignment help</a></h3>
            <p class="level-qual">{lvl.title}</p>
            <ul class="level-meta">
              <li><span class="meta-key">Units:</span> {lvl.units}</li>
              <li><span class="meta-key">Format:</span> {lvl.format}</li>
              <li><span class="meta-key">Command verbs:</span> {lvl.verbs}</li>
              <li><span class="meta-key">Student profile:</span> {lvl.profile}</li>
            </ul>
            <span class="level-link" aria-hidden="true">View {lvl.label} units →</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       HOW IT WORKS — WhatsApp process
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="how-cmi-assignment-help-works">How Ordering Works, Step by Step</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        The entire process runs through WhatsApp, from initial quote to final delivery. No registration, no portals.
      </p>
      <div class="steps-grid">
        {steps.map(step => (
          <div class="step-card">
            <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">{step.n}</span>
            <p class="step-text">{step.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="steps-cta">
        <a
          href={whatsappUrl}
          class="btn btn-whatsapp btn-lg"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Start on WhatsApp
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       WRITER CREDIBILITY — trust signals
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="uk-based-cmi-qualified-writers">Who Works on Your Assignment</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Every CMI assignment is written by a practitioner who holds the CMI qualification at the level they write,
        not a generalist academic writer.
      </p>
      <div class="cred-grid">
        <div class="cred-card tone-blue">
          <span class="badge-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg class="svc-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false" set:html={serviceIcons.award}></svg>
          </span>
          <h3 class="cred-title">Qualification Match</h3>
          <p>
            Writers hold current CMI qualifications at the level they are assigned. A Level 7 strategic paper is
            written by a CMI Level 7 holder, not by a Level 5 practitioner writing upward.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="cred-card tone-purple">
          <span class="badge-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg class="svc-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false" set:html={serviceIcons.target}></svg>
          </span>
          <h3 class="cred-title">Command Verb Expertise</h3>
          <p>
            Every response is calibrated to the exact command verb in your brief. Critically appraise at Level 7
            requires different argumentation depth, source weight, and structural positioning than Evaluate at Level 5.
            Our writers know the difference and write to assessor expectations.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="cred-card tone-pink">
          <span class="badge-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg class="svc-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false" set:html={serviceIcons.pin}></svg>
          </span>
          <h3 class="cred-title">UK Sector Experience</h3>
          <p>
            Writers are UK-based management practitioners, NHS leaders, public sector managers, commercial directors,
            and professional services leaders. CMI qualification content is grounded in UK management context;
            our writers reflect that.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="cred-card tone-orange">
          <span class="badge-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg class="svc-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false" set:html={serviceIcons.book}></svg>
          </span>
          <h3 class="cred-title">Harvard Referencing to CMI Standards</h3>
          <p>
            All assignments use Harvard referencing with credible sources chosen to support each criterion,
            including CMI's ManagementDirect where it is relevant. The unit specifications don't set a minimum number of sources, so your centre's brief and referencing guidance apply.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       FAQ — contextual border (macro → supplementary)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container faq-wrap">
      <h2 class="section-title faq-title" id="cmi-assignment-help-faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p class="section-lead faq-lead">Quick answers on levels, grading, referencing, resubmissions and ordering.</p>

      <div class="faq-tabbed" id="faq-tabbed">
        <div class="faq-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="FAQ categories">
          {faqGroups.map((group, i) => (
            <button
              type="button"
              role="tab"
              class="faq-tab"
              id={`faq-tab-${group.id}`}
              aria-controls={`faq-panel-${group.id}`}
              aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
              tabindex={i === 0 ? 0 : -1}
            >{group.label}</button>
          ))}
        </div>

        {faqGroups.map((group, i) => (
          <div
            class={`faq-panel${i === 0 ? ' is-active' : ''}`}
            role="tabpanel"
            id={`faq-panel-${group.id}`}
            aria-labelledby={`faq-tab-${group.id}`}
          >
            <h3 class="faq-cat">{group.label}</h3>
            <div class="faq-list">
              {group.items.map((item) => (
                <details class="faq-item">
                  <summary class="faq-q">{item.q}</summary>
                  <div class="faq-a">
                    {item.a.map((para) => (
                      <p>{para.map((part) => (typeof part === 'string' ? part : <a href={part.href}>{part.text}</a>))}</p>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                </details>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <!-- Tabs are added only when JavaScript runs. Without it, every question shows in one list under its category name. -->
      <script is:inline>
        (function () {
          var root = document.getElementById('faq-tabbed');
          if (!root) return;
          var tabs = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[role="tab"]'));
          var panels = tabs.map(function (tab) { return document.getElementById(tab.getAttribute('aria-controls')); });

          function select(index, moveFocus) {
            tabs.forEach(function (tab, n) {
              var isOn = n === index;
              tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', isOn ? 'true' : 'false');
              tab.tabIndex = isOn ? 0 : -1;
              panels[n].classList.toggle('is-active', isOn);
            });
            if (moveFocus) tabs[index].focus();
          }

          tabs.forEach(function (tab, index) {
            tab.addEventListener('click', function () { select(index, false); });
            tab.addEventListener('keydown', function (event) {
              var next = null;
              if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') next = (index + 1) % tabs.length;
              else if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft') next = (index - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
              else if (event.key === 'Home') next = 0;
              else if (event.key === 'End') next = tabs.length - 1;
              if (next === null) return;
              event.preventDefault();
              select(next, true);
            });
          });

          root.classList.add('faq-js');
        })();
      </script>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       FINAL CTA
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section cta-section">
    <div class="container cta-inner">
      <h2 class="cta-h2">Get a Quote Today</h2>
      <p class="cta-sub">
